# 4. SUBARRAY WITH GIVEN SUM

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

## PROBLEM

Find whether a contiguous subarray has sum:

```
K
```

Example:

```
[1,4,20,3,10,5]
```

K:

```
33
```

Subarray:

```
20 + 3 + 10 = 33
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## IMPORTANT CONDITION

The simple sliding-window solution works when:

```
all numbers are NON-NEGATIVE
```

This distinction is critical.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## WHY?

With non-negative numbers:

If current sum becomes too large:

```
remove from left
```

If too small:

```
expand right
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## TEMPLATE

```
left = 0
sum = 0

for right:

    sum += a[right]

    while(sum > K):

        sum -= a[left]
        left++

    if(sum == K)
        found
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## CODE

```
long long sum = 0;

int left = 0;

for(int right = 0;
    right < n;
    right++) {

    sum += a[right];

    while(sum > k &&
          left <= right) {

        sum -= a[left];

        left++;
    }

    if(sum == k) {

        cout << "YES";
        return;
    }
}

cout << "NO";
```

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## WARNING

If negative values exist:

```
DO NOT automatically use
this sliding window.
```

Use:

```
PREFIX SUM + HASHMAP
```

instead.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

## RECOGNITION

```
